+++ b/docs/patches/0117-plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Patch 0117: Routegraph walk repeat (show "xN" when a control is used more than once)
+
+Stacks on 0116. Not a training course: this lets a fix or a walk carry the number of times a control is used in a row, and shows it. The living plan and log is `docs/ROUTEGRAPH_GUIDANCE.md`.
+
+## What you asked
+> do all of the above :3 lets start with 1-4
+
+This is item 3 of the "Still to do" list (the dock's `repeat`). Item 1 was already answered (`src/lib/trainingSandbox.ts`), item 2 landed in 0116, and item 4 is deferred on purpose (see below).
+
+## How it works
+- **A fix can ask for more than one press.** `FixCandidate` (`src/lib/trainingCourse.ts`) gained `repeat?: number`, and the qty deviation puts its count on the window fix (`repeat: extra`), where `extra` is how many units too many there are. So "three items where one is enough" carries `repeat: 2`.
+- **The graph can too.** `RuntimeSpot` (`src/lib/appGraph.ts`) gained `repeat`, which rides on the action node (`registerActions` accepts `repeat`). routegraph resolves it onto the instruction action (`InstructionAction.repeat`), and `candidateFromStep` reads it back, so a walk with a repeat comes out as one step with a count, not repeated steps.
+- **The dock shows it.** `DockView` (`src/state/trainingSession.ts`) gained `repeat`; `TrainingHost` carries it from the chosen candidate; `TrainingDock` draws a small `xN` chip beside the counter. The words are untouched: the qty fix already says "take two out", so this is the count beside them, not a replacement.
+- **Tests**: `tests/trainingcourse.test.ts` (the qty window fix carries the count, the plain swipe does not); `tests/appnavgraph.test.ts` (a runtime control's repeat rides on the planned step, not as repeated steps).
+
+## Not covered
+Item 4 (moving the control-to-screen table's last rough edges onto screen metadata) is deferred, and the reason is now written down: it needs the graph to know *which* window is open (like `openLine` does for a line window). Today every sheet folds into the page under it, so listing a sheet control on the tab is deliberate; moving it onto the sheet now would make the graph add a spurious "open the window" step while it is already open. That is hidden behind the plain answer today, but it is wrong, and it would surface the moment the graph leads. Items 5-7 (device tests, the next course, the stashes) are unchanged.
+
+## Checklist
+1. [x] `src/lib/trainingCourse.ts`: `Deviation.window.repeat`, `FixCandidate.repeat`, the qty window carries the count.
+2. [x] `src/lib/appGraph.ts`: `RuntimeSpot.repeat`, `repeatOfStep`, `candidateFromStep`.
+3. [x] `src/state/trainingSession.ts`, `src/ui/TrainingHost.tsx`, `src/ui/TrainingDock.tsx`: carry and draw `repeat`.
+4. [x] Tests: `tests/trainingcourse.test.ts`, `tests/appnavgraph.test.ts`.
+5. [x] `npm run typecheck` clean; full suite (the one failure is pre-existing on `origin/main`: `tests/virtualterminal.test.ts`, "every screen has copy...").
+6. [x] `docs/ROUTEGRAPH_GUIDANCE.md` (living plan/log).
